-- patterns.talk: the pattern-size-minimum case. `<99999 digits>` compiles to
-- 99999 `class digit` and a `match`: 100000 instructions, loaded as a
-- constant. The spliced patterns are compiled at their `make-pattern`.

on build extra
  put <99999 digits> into p
  if extra then
    put <(p), digit> into q
  else
    put <(p)> into q
  end if
  return "built"
end build
